Split across covers
Spread one message across all the selected cover files (one stego image per cover, written to the output folder) instead of embedding the same message into each. Needs at least two covers and a folder as the output.
Options
Algorithm
Encryption algorithm
Password
Confirm password
Algorithm options
SI-UNIWARD — JPEG, strongest at low rates
Adaptive — PNG, most secure
LSB matching — PNG, higher capacity
Random LSB — PNG, high capacity
LSB — PNG, legacy
WAV LSB — audio, lossless PCM
<html><b>SI-UNIWARD (JPEG)</b><br>Content-adaptive embedding that hides data in JPEG coefficients, concentrating changes in noisy, hard-to-model regions.<br><br><b>Format:</b> JPEG &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> low &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> lowest<br><i>Best when secrecy matters most and the payload is small.</i></html>
<html><b>Adaptive (PNG)</b><br>Steers embedding toward busy, high-variance pixels where changes are hardest to detect, while keeping output lossless.<br><br><b>Format:</b> PNG &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> moderate &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> low<br><i>The most secure lossless option — a strong general-purpose default.</i></html>
<html><b>LSB matching (PNG)</b><br>Randomly spreads the payload across pixels, incrementing/decrementing values rather than overwriting the last bit — harder to detect than plain LSB.<br><br><b>Format:</b> PNG &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> high &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> moderate<br><i>Good balance of capacity and stealth.</i></html>
<html><b>Random LSB (PNG)</b><br>Overwrites least-significant bits at pseudo-random, password-seeded positions across the image.<br><br><b>Format:</b> PNG &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> high &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> higher<br><i>Use when you need to fit a large payload and detectability is less of a concern.</i></html>
<html><b>LSB (PNG)</b><br>Classic sequential least-significant-bit embedding. Simple and high-capacity, but the easiest to detect.<br><br><b>Format:</b> PNG &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> highest &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> highest<br><i>Legacy/compatibility option — prefer the others for real secrecy.</i></html>
<html><b>WAV LSB (audio)</b><br>Hides data in the least-significant bit of each integer PCM sample of an uncompressed WAV. Output is a same-format WAV that still plays normally.<br><br><b>Format:</b> WAV (lossless PCM) &nbsp; <b>Capacity:</b> high &nbsp; <b>Detectability:</b> higher<br><i>For hiding data in audio. Lossy formats (MP3, AAC) cannot carry LSB data.</i></html>
